    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "In how many ways can three different Maths books, six different Science books and four different English books be placed on a shelf, if the books relating to each subject are to be kept together?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$622\\,080$",
      "worked": "Treat each subject as one unit. Arrange the three subject units in $3!$ ways, then rearrange the books within each subject in $3!$, $6!$ and $4!$ ways respectively.\n\n$\\begin{aligned}N&=3!\\times3!\\times6!\\times4!\\\\&=622\\,080\\end{aligned}$",
